\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Seek him that made the Pleiades and Orion, that turneth deep\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 darkness into the morning, and darkeneth the day into night;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 that calleth for the waters of the sea, and poureth them out\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 upon the face of the earth:  The Lord is his Name.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Amos 5:8}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 If I say, "Surely the darkness will cover me, and the light\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 around me turn to night," darkness is not dark to thee, O \softline
Lord;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 the night is as bright as the day; darkness and light to thee\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 are both alike.  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Psalm 139:10,11}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Jesus said, "I am the light of the world; he that followeth me\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life."\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 John 8:12}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The following Confession of Sin may then be said; or the Office may\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 continue at once with {\u8220\'93}O God make speed to save us.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 {\u8221\'94}\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \b\f1 Confession of Sin}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The Officiant says to the people}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Dear friends in Christ, here in the presence of Almighty God,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 let us kneel in silence, and with penitent and obedient hearts\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 confess our sins, so that we may obtain forgiveness by his\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 infinite goodness and mercy.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 or this}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Let us humbly confess our sins unto Almighty God. \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Silence may be kept.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Officiant and People together, all kneeling}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Almighty and most merciful Father,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 we have erred and strayed from thy ways like lost sheep,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 we have followed too much the devices and desires of our\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1     own hearts,\par
}\column 
\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 we have offended against thy holy laws,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 we have left undone those things which we ought to\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1     have done,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and we have done those things which we ought not to\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1     have done.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 But thou, O Lord, have mercy upon us,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 spare thou those who confess their faults,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 restore thou those who are penitent,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 according to thy promises declared unto mankind\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 in Christ Jesus our Lord;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and grant, O most merciful Father, for his sake,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 that we may hereafter live a godly, righteous, and sober life,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 to the glory of thy holy Name.  Amen.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The Priest alone stands and says}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 The Almighty and merciful Lord grant you absolution and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 remission of all your sins, true repentance, amendment of\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 life, and the grace and consolation of his Holy Spirit.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 Amen.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 \par
}\pard \fs20
